  "summary": "The code contained a critical SSTI vulnerability due to unsafe template string concatenation, alongside maintainability issues regarding documentation and type safety. I have refactored the code to use a secure template rendering approach and added necessary type hints and input validation to improve robustness.",
  "fixed_code": "from flask import Flask, render_template, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\ndef format_total(cents: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Formats an integer amount in cents to a string representation of dollars.\"\"\"\n    return f\"{cents / 100:.2f}\"\n\n@app.route(\"/confirmation\")\ndef confirmation():\n    note = request.args.get(\"note\", \"\")\n    try:\n        cents_raw = request.args.get(\"cents\", 0)\n        total = format_total(int(cents_raw))\n    except (ValueError, TypeError):\n        return \"Invalid total amount\", 400\n\n    # Assuming a file named templates/confirmation.html exists\n    return render_template(\"confirmation.html\", note=note, total=total)"
